/// What the kernel hands the automation worker for a trigger that matched an event and starts no run for a reason that is recorded (D-7200, SCH-1532): the trigger and its automation, the event sequence, its hop count, the reason (hop-limit, run-as-suspended, automation-removed or condition-failed) and a detail of at most 256 characters that names ids and limits only, never a field value. The worker writes it as a declined rec-automation-exception in the commit of the transition. Carried by the effect decline-automation.
